<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title><![CDATA[Spring]]></title><description><![CDATA[Level up your Java code and explore what Spring can do for you.]]></description><link>https://spring.io</link><generator>GatsbyJS</generator><lastBuildDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 08:52:00 GMT</lastBuildDate><item><title><![CDATA[This Week in Spring - June 9th, 2026]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/09/this-week-in-spring-june-9-2026</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/09/this-week-in-spring-june-9-2026</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[joshlong]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;Hi Spring fans! Welcome to another installment of &lt;em&gt;This Week in Spring&lt;/em&gt;! Tons of releases coming out today and this week! So make sure you&apos;re pulling in the latest posts, as often as possible!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-ldap-releases-2026-06&quot;&gt;Spring LDAP 2026.06 Releases - Contains CVE Fix&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-framework-7-0-8-and-6-2-19-available-now&quot;&gt;Spring Framework 7.0.8 and 6.2.19 Available Now&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-hateoas-3-1-GA-3-0-7-and-2-5-3-released&quot;&gt;Spring HATEOAS 3.1 GA, 3.0.7, and 2.5.3 released&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-retry-2&quot;&gt;Spring Retry 2.0.13 available now&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/06/spring-ai-2-0-0-RC1-available-now&quot;&gt;Spring AI RC1 is available now&lt;/a&gt;. This release includes a well overhauled tool calling approach, chat memory improvements, structured output enhancements, and so much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;as part of these new releases, you may have noticed, we&apos;ve addressed &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.infoworld.com/article/4182556/broadcom-beefs-up-spring-security-to-protect-against-ai-enabled-attacks.html&quot;&gt;many CVEs&lt;/a&gt;. Make sure you update now!  We revealed yesterday that the number of monthly security advisories reported to Broadcom by he Spring community increased by more than 1,700% from March to April of this year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=khtzn_VkGsw&quot;&gt;my talk at JNation looking at Spring Boot 4 is available now&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/advance-java/how-spring-boot-application-works-internally/&quot;&gt;interesting look at how Spring Boot works internally&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spring LDAP 2026.06 Releases - Contains CVE Fix]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-ldap-releases-2026-06</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-ldap-releases-2026-06</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[jzheaux]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;On behalf of the team and everyone who has contributed, I am pleased to announce the availability of Spring LDAP &lt;code&gt;3.3.8&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;4.0.4&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;4.1.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These releases address the following CVE:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41720&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-41720&lt;/a&gt; &quot;Authentication Bypass with Empty Password in Spring LDAP&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the &lt;code&gt;4.1.0&lt;/code&gt; release, please check out the main feature set in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.spring.io/spring-ldap/reference/4.1/whats-new.html&quot;&gt;What&apos;s New in Spring LDAP 4.1 page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a complete list of changes, refer to the changelogs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ldap/releases/tag/3.3.8&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;3.3.8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ldap/releases/tag/4.0.4&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;4.0.4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ldap/releases/tag/4.1.0&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;4.1.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;commercial-releases&quot; style=&quot;position:relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#commercial-releases&quot; aria-label=&quot;commercial releases permalink&quot; class=&quot;anchor before&quot;&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; focusable=&quot;false&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; version=&quot;1.1&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Commercial Releases&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open source support for Spring LDAP 2.4.x and 3.2.x generations has ended, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-ldap#support&quot;&gt;our support page for more information&lt;/a&gt;.
Commercial customers can update to &lt;code&gt;2.4.5&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;3.2.18&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;3.3.7.1&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;4.0.3.1&lt;/code&gt; respectively.
These are also included in the latest Boot releases, &lt;code&gt;2.7.34&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;3.3.20&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;3.4.17&lt;/code&gt;, as well as Boot hot fixes &lt;code&gt;3.5.14.1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;4.0.6.1&lt;/code&gt;.
These versions are available now on the Spring commercial artifact repository and can be accessed with a &lt;a href=&quot;https://enterprise.spring.io&quot;&gt;Spring Enterprise Subscription&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-ldap/&quot;&gt;Project Page&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ldap&quot;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-ldap/issues&quot;&gt;Issues&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.spring.io/spring-ldap/reference/&quot;&gt;Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spring HATEOAS 3.1 GA, 3.0.7, and 2.5.3 released]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-hateoas-3-1-GA-3-0-7-and-2-5-3-released</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-hateoas-3-1-GA-3-0-7-and-2-5-3-released</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[odrotbohm]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;On behalf of the community, I am excited to announce the availability of Spring HATEOAS 3.1 GA, 3.0.7, 2.5.3. The GA release ships the usual dependency updates and a few polishes in link parsing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;cve-reports&quot; style=&quot;position:relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#cve-reports&quot; aria-label=&quot;cve reports permalink&quot; class=&quot;anchor before&quot;&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; focusable=&quot;false&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; version=&quot;1.1&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;CVE reports&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These releases address the following CVEs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41006&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-41006&lt;/a&gt; – Spring HATEOAS Collection+JSON/UBER deserializers do not honor Jackson configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41007&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-41007&lt;/a&gt; – Spring HATEOAS heap exhaustion through unbounded internal caching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find more information in the full changelogs for &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-hateoas/releases/tag/3.1.0&quot;&gt;3.1 GA&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-hateoas/releases/tag/3.0.7&quot;&gt;3.0.7&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-hateoas/releases/tag/2.5.3&quot;&gt;2.5.3&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spring Retry 2.0.13 available now]]></title><link>https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-retry-2</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://spring.io/blog/2026/06/08/spring-retry-2</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[snicoll]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 08 Jun 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><content:encoded>&lt;p&gt;On behalf of the team and everyone who has contributed, I&apos;m happy to announce that Spring Retry &lt;code&gt;2.0.13&lt;/code&gt; has been released and is now available from Maven Central.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This release includes &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-retry/releases/tag/v2.0.13&quot;&gt;5 bug fixes, documentation improvements, and dependency upgrades&lt;/a&gt;. Thanks to all those who have contributed with issue reports and pull requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;cve-reports&quot; style=&quot;position:relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#cve-reports&quot; aria-label=&quot;cve reports permalink&quot; class=&quot;anchor before&quot;&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; focusable=&quot;false&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; version=&quot;1.1&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;CVE reports&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This release addresses a CVE:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/security/cve-2026-41710&quot;&gt;CVE-2026-41710&lt;/a&gt; &quot;Cache Exhaustion in Stateful Retries leads to Denial of Service&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;how-can-you-help&quot; style=&quot;position:relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#how-can-you-help&quot; aria-label=&quot;how can you help permalink&quot; class=&quot;anchor before&quot;&gt;&lt;svg aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; focusable=&quot;false&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; version=&quot;1.1&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 16 16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;How can you help?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&apos;re interested in helping out, check out the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-retry/labels/status%3A%20ideal-for-contribution&quot;&gt;&quot;ideal for contribution&quot; tag&lt;/a&gt; in the issue repository. If you have general questions, please ask on &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com&quot;&gt;stackoverflow.com&lt;/a&gt; using the &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/tags/spring-retry&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;spring-retry&lt;/code&gt; tag&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://spring.io/projects/spring-retry/&quot;&gt;Project Page&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-retry&quot;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-retry/issues&quot;&gt;Issues&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/spring-retry&quot;&gt;Stack Overflow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded></item></channel></rss>